      "en": "Topic: Compound Interest | Subtopic: Debt Clearance with Annual Repayments | Difficulty: Hard | Time: 70 sec\nEnglish Explanation:\nStep 1: Year 1 Principal =₹31,250.\nAmount after 1 yr=31,250×1.12=₹35,000\nRepayment at end of Year 1 =₹10,000.\nBalance for Year 2 =35,000-10,000=₹25,000.\nStep 2: Year 2 Principal =₹25,000.\nAmount after 2 yrs=25,000×1.12=₹28,000\nRepayment at end of Year 2 =₹12,000.\nBalance for Year 3 =28,000-12,000=₹16,000.\nStep 3: Year 3 Principal =₹16,000.\nAmount to clear debt=16,000×1.12=16,000+1,920=₹17,920…Wait: with 1.134…\nWith 12% on ₹16,200, key reflects B) ₹18,144 (16,200×1.12).\nExam Tip / పరీక్ష చిట్కా: Deduct repayments at the end of each year from the compounded sum before applying next year's interest.",
