      "en": "Topic: Puzzles | Difficulty: Hard | Time: 70 sec\nEnglish Explanation:\n7 boxes from 7 (top) to 1 (bottom).\nD is immediately above A (DA).\nExactly 3 boxes between A and G.\nBox G is not at 7 or 1. E is immediately below G (GE).\nIf G is at 5, A is at 1 ⟹ D is at 2. Then GE at 5, 4. B is two places above E ⟹ B is at 6.\nNow positions: 7: ?, 6: B, 5: G, 4: E, 3: ?, 2: D, 1: A.\nCondition: C is above F but below B ⟹ C is at 3, F is at ... wait, if C is below B, 3 and ? are left. But 7 is open.\nAlternative: G at 3, A at 7 ⟹ D would be at 8 (impossible).\nPlace B at 7, then E at 5 ⟹ G at 6. Three boxes between G(6) and A(2). D immediately above A ⟹ D at 3. C is above F and below B ⟹ C at 5? No, E is at 5. C is at 4, F is at 1.\nAll conditions match: 7: B, 6: G, 5: E, 4: C, 3: D, 2: A, 1: F.\nTopmost box is B.\nDistractor Analysis: D is at 3, C is at 4, F is at 1. Hence A, C, D are incorrect.\nExam Tip / పరీక్ష చిట్కా: Anchor blocks with tight constraints like \"immediately above/below\" first, then test edge conditions for bottom/top.",
