      "en": "Topic: Direction Sense | Difficulty: Moderate | Time: 50 sec\nEnglish Explanation:\nUsing Cartesian coordinates with A at (0,0):\n1. East 12 m →(12,0).\n2. Right turn (South) 8 m to B →(12,-8).\n3. Left turn (East) 6 m →(18,-8).\n4. Left turn (North) 20 m to C →(18,12).\n5. Left turn (West) 18 m to D →(18-18,12)=(0,12).\nShortest distance between A (0,0) and D (0,12)=√((0-0)^(2)+(12-0)^(2))=12 metres.\nDistractor Analysis: 10, 15, and 8 arise from forgetting the 6 m eastward offset or subtracting 8 from 20 incorrectly.\nExam Tip / పరీక్ష చిట్కా: Convert multi-turn direction questions into (x,y) coordinates to avoid diagram clutter and calculate final displacement instantly.",
