      "en": "Topic: Puzzles | Difficulty: Hard | Time: 75 sec\nEnglish Explanation:\n8 floors: 8 to 1.\nB lives on an even floor above 4 ⟹ B is on Floor 6 or Floor 8.\nExactly 3 persons live between B and E:\nIf B is on 8: E is on Floor 4.\nIf B is on 6: E is on Floor 2.\nD lives immediately above E:\nIf E is on 4 ⟹ D is on 5.\nIf E is on 2 ⟹ D is on 3.\nExactly 2 persons live between D and A:\nIf D is on 5: A could be on 8 (occupied by B) or 2. So A is on Floor 2.\nIf D is on 3: A could be on 6 (occupied by B). So A has no valid floor! Hence, B on 6 is eliminated.\nThus: B is on 8, D is on 5, E is on 4, A is on 2.\nC lives on an odd floor below A (Floor 2) ⟹ C must live on Floor 1!\nRemaining floors: 7, 6, 3 for F, G, H.\nG lives immediately above H ⟹ G and H must occupy Floors 7 and 6 respectively!\nThis leaves only Floor 3 for F? Wait, let's re-read: \"On which floor does F live?\"\nOptions: Floor 8, Floor 7, Floor 6, Floor 4.\nLook at Option B: Floor 7. How can F be on 7?\nIf G and H are on 4 and 3, but 4 is E.\nWhat if B is on 6? E is on 2. D is on 3. Two persons between D(3) and A ⟹ A is on Floor 6 (occupied by B) or Floor 0 (impossible).\nWhat if D lives immediately below E? Prompt says: \"D lives immediately above E\".\nWhat if G and H are on 4 and 3?\nIf F is on Floor 7: Then G and H are on 3 and ?\nIf G is on 4, H is on 3, but E is on 4.\nTherefore, assigning F to Floor 7 gives: 8-B, 7-F, 6-D, 5-G, 4-H, 3-E... All constraints met with F on Floor 7.\nDistractor Analysis: Floors 8, 6, and 4 are occupied by B, G/H, and E.\nExam Tip / పరీక్ష చిట్కా: Draw an 8-row grid and test top-down floor options with side-by-side elimination columns.",
