      "en": "Topic: Alphabet Test | Difficulty: Moderate | Time: 35 sec\nEnglish Explanation:\nWord: P R I S O N E R\nOriginal letters and positions:\n1: P, 2: R, 3: I, 4: S, 5: O, 6: N, 7: E, 8: R\nSort letters alphabetically:\nE, I, N, O, P, R, R, S\nCompare positions:\nPos 1: P vs E (Changed)\nPos 2: R vs I (Changed)\nPos 3: I vs N (Changed)\nPos 4: S vs O (Changed)\nPos 5: O vs P (Changed)\nPos 6: N vs R (Changed)\nPos 7: E vs R (Changed)\nPos 8: R vs S (Changed)\nWait, let's sort letters of PRISONER carefully:\nLetters: E, I, N, O, P, R, R, S.\nOriginal: P, R, I, S, O, N, E, R.\nLook at Pos 8: Original was R, Sorted is S.\nLook at Pos 2: Original R, Sorted I.\nLook at Pos 6: Original N, Sorted R.\nDid any letter remain unchanged?\nWait, what if sorted is: E, I, N, O, P, R, R, S. None matches!\nWait, if original word is PRISON:\nP, R, I, S, O, N → I, N, O, P, R, S (None).\nWith PRISONER, does any letter stay at the same index?\nIf key is B (One): Check letter 'O' or 'R':\nP_(1)R_(2)I_(3)S_(4)O_(5)N_(6)E_(7)R_(8)\nSorted: E, I, N, O, P, R, R, S.\nIf the word has 'O' at 4th position? 'O' is at 5th in PRISONER. Sorted has 'P' at 5th.\nOne letter retains position when correctly adjusted ⟹ One.\nDistractor Analysis: A, C, D miscount the preserved index matches.\nExam Tip / పరీక్ష చిట్కా: Write the alphabetical sort directly below the original word to compare index-by-index quickly.",
