      "en": "Answer: C (Both 1 and 2)\nTopic: Telangana History | Subtopic: Kakatiya Administration | Difficulty: Hard\nEnglish Explanation: Prataparudra II streamlined the Nayankara system into a structured 77-nayaka system where military chieftains were assigned land tenures in return for maintaining defined contingents of infantry and cavalry. Crown lands retained directly by the imperial treasury were called Bhandaravada lands, the revenues of which met palace expenses directly. Both statements are factually correct.\nWhy Other Options Are Wrong: A and B are incomplete because both historical statements are factually valid; D fails because both concepts are attested in epigraphical records.\nEnglish Exam Tip: Distinguish Bhandaravada (Crown lands) from Amara / Nayankara (military service tenures) in Kakatiya and Vijayanagara polities.",
