      "en": "Answer: C (1975)\nTopic: Telangana Movement | Subtopic: Presidential Order (Art 371D) | Difficulty: Moderate\nEnglish Explanation: In exercise of the powers conferred by clauses (1) and (2) of Article 371D of the Constitution, the President of India issued the Andhra Pradesh Public Employment (Organisation of Local Cadres and Regulation of Direct Recruitment) Order, 1975 on 20th October 1975. It classified local cadres into zones and reserved non-gazetted direct recruitment posts for locals.\nWhy Other Options Are Wrong: 1973 was the year of the 32nd Constitutional Amendment Act; 1974 saw the formal notification of the Six-Point Formula principles; 1978 relates to secondary departmental rules.\nEnglish Exam Tip: Remember: 32nd Amendment was passed in 1973; the resultant Presidential Order was issued on 20 October 1975.",
