      "en": "Answer: C (Justice Fazal Ali)\nTopic: Telangana Movement | Subtopic: States Reorganisation Commission (1953) | Difficulty: Easy\nEnglish Explanation: The States Reorganisation Commission (SRC), appointed by the Government of India in December 1953, was chaired by former Supreme Court judge Justice Fazal Ali (along with members Kavalam Madhava Panikkar and Hriday Nath Kunzru). In Paragraphs 378–389 of its report submitted in 1955, the commission cautioned against immediate integration and recommended that Telangana be constituted as a separate State (Hyderabad State), with unification with Andhra left to a two-thirds majority decision of the Telangana legislature after the 1961 general elections.\nWhy Other Options Are Wrong: Panikkar and Kunzru were members, not the Chairman; Pattabhi Sitaramayya was a member of the earlier 1948 JVP Committee.\nEnglish Exam Tip: Fazal Ali Commission (SRC 1953) explicitly warned that unification would economically and educationally disadvantage Telangana and recommended retaining a separate Telangana state.",
